Why: patch 0010 tracks the one OUTPUT buffer the encoder firmware currently owns,
so that a firmware result error can return it from the vb2 queue directly rather
than through v4l2_m2m_src_buf_remove(), which cannot find it (start_encode has
already taken it off the ready queue). This adds the field that holds it.

Separate from 0010 only because its context depends on patch 0014: the field sits
beside keep_dma_bufs, which 0014 introduces, so the hunk cannot apply before it.
Patch order is not compile order; only the final tree is built.

--- a/drivers/media/platform/chips-media/wave5/wave5-vpuapi.h
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/chips-media/wave5/wave5-vpuapi.h
@@ -819,6 +819,7 @@
 	bool nv21;
 	bool eos;
 	bool keep_dma_bufs;
+	s32 active_enc_src_idx;
 	struct vpu_buf bitstream_vbuf;
 	dma_addr_t last_rd_ptr;
 	size_t remaining_consumed_bytes;
